I am testing open:creib.forge.conformance.oracle.recover_json_object. The documented rule says: "The object scored is the last one inside a code fence when any fence holds one, else the last top-level object in the text." Reply A is "```json\n{\"a\":1}\n```\n~~~\n{\"b\":2}\n~~~"; Reply B is "```json\n{\"a\":1}\n```". The rule requires A to score {"b":2}, because the tilde fence is a code fence and it is the last fence holding an object; the rule requires B to score {"a":1}, because that is the only fenced object. But recover_json_object returns {"a":1} for both, because its fence regex only recognizes backtick fences and ignores the tilde fence, so for A it never sees the tilde-fenced object and falls back to the last backtick-fenced object. I would be wrong if recover_json_object returns {"b":2} for A and {"a":1} for B, or if the documented rule is read as excluding tilde fences from "code fence".